<!doctype html>
{%- comment -%}
  Reading direction. Liquid has no request.locale.direction, so the RTL
  locales are listed explicitly. Without dir the browser lays every
  locale out left-to-right, and the logical properties in kj-v2.css —
  inset-inline, padding-inline, text-align:start — have nothing to
  mirror against. Urdu is the realistic case for this shop; ar/he/fa
  are here because the list costs nothing.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign rtl_locales = 'ar,arc,ckb,dv,fa,ha,he,khw,ks,ku,ps,sd,ur,uz-AF,yi' | split: ','
  assign lang = request.locale.iso_code
  assign base = lang | split: '-' | first
  assign dir = 'ltr'
  for code in rtl_locales
    if code == lang or code == base
      assign dir = 'rtl'
    endif
  endfor
-%}
<html lang="{{ lang }}" dir="{{ dir }}">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>{{ page_title }}{% if page_title != shop.name %} &mdash; {{ shop.name }}{% endif %}</title>
{% if page_description %}<meta name="description" content="{{ page_description }}">{% endif %}
<link rel="canonical" href="{{ canonical_url }}">
{%- comment -%}
  One preload, because the site is now one typeface. Montserrat's
  variable latin file covers every weight the theme asks for, so
  preloading it covers the header, the hero and all body copy. Archivo,
  Archivo Black, Bodoni Moda and Italianno are still served by fonts.css
  for anything that still asks for them, but nothing above the fold does,
  so preloading them was costing three requests for no paint.
{%- endcomment -%}
{{ 'montserrat-latin.woff2' | asset_url | preload_tag: as: 'font', type: 'font/woff2', crossorigin: 'anonymous' }}
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ 'fonts.css' | asset_url }}">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ 'site.css' | asset_url }}">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="{{ 'kj-v2.css' | asset_url }}">
{{ content_for_header }}
</head>
{%- comment -%}
  The body carried no class at all, so nothing on the page could ask
  "which template am I on". That is fine until a template needs its own
  register: the Lada page wants the header transparent over its hero
  plate and solid once scrolled, and there was no hook to scope that to
  Lada without leaking it onto every other page.

  Standard Shopify shape: `template-page` plus `template-page-lada` for
  a page.lada.json template. Additive only, so nothing that already
  matched on a bare <body> changes.
{%- endcomment -%}
<body class="template-{{ template.name }}{% if template.suffix %} template-{{ template.name }}-{{ template.suffix }}{% endif %}">
<a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
{% render 'kj-svg-defs' %}

{% section 'header' %}

<main id="main">
{{ content_for_layout }}
</main>

{% section 'footer' %}

{%- comment -%}
  The bag lives in the layout so it can open from any page, and so the
  Section Rendering API has a stable target to re-render after every
  cart change.
{%- endcomment -%}
{% section 'kj-cart-drawer' %}

<script src="{{ 'site.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
<script src="{{ 'kj-v2.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
<script src="{{ 'kj-cart.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
</body>
</html>
